      "title": "Russia is ‘setting traps’ in Ukraine talks, EU foreign policy chief warns",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/13/russia-ukraine-talks-kaja-kallas-eu-foreign-policy-dublin-summit",
      "description": "<p>Kaja Kallas says Moscow is trying to divert attention from its aggression by raising issue of European security</p><p>The EU’s foreign policy chief has warned against “walking into the traps that Russia is setting” as she said Moscow was trying to start a debate about European security in order to divert attention from its aggression.</p><p>“We have one aggressor and one victim, and the aggressor does not have security concerns,” Kaja Kallas said on arrival at an EU leaders’ summit in Dublin. “Nobody has ever attacked them. They have attacked others. I mean, keep the focus, people.”</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/13/russia-ukraine-talks-kaja-kallas-eu-foreign-policy-dublin-summit\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-13T20:38:25"
    },
    {
      "title": "Europe to send diplomat team to Ukraine talks as leaders push for a voice",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/europe-to-send-diplomat-team-to-ukraine-talks-as-leaders-push-for-a-voice-126111400007_1.html",
      "description": "Europe will send a team of diplomats from across the continent to Ukraine peace talks, the European Union announced Friday.\nEuropean Council President Antonio Costa said the continent would be represented by the EU and five members of the \"coalition of the willing\" that backs Ukraine: the UK, France, Germany, Italy and Poland.\nHe spoke at the end of a summit of EU leaders in Dublin dominated by how Europe can play a role to bolster Ukraine, and protect its own security, in US-backed negotiations with Moscow and Kyiv on ending the almost five-year war.\nEuropean leaders have been concerned that a US-backed process will leave them sidelined and Kyiv vulnerable as Moscow and Washington decide the fate of a conflict that has roiled the continent.\nUkraine is eager for support from its European allies. It's reluctant to leave the talks solely in the hands of a US administration that has often seemed to lean toward Moscow's views. Russia does not want European countries involved in direct",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-14T02:29:27"
    }
